/usr/sbin/dump -0uf /dev/nrmt0h /dev/rrz3g
/usr/sbin/dump -1uf /dev/nrmt0h /dev/rrz2c
rsh quigley /usr/sbin/rdump -1uf spectre:/dev/nrmt0h /dev/rrz2g
rsh quigley /usr/sbin/rdump -1uf spectre:/dev/rmt0h /dev/rrz1c

When the backups are done using a direct connect DAT drive (same drive),
they run just fine.

Has anyone seen any problems running a remote backup on DEC Unix 4.0?

