> remove the menu bar (preferably from .Xdefaults).

It's not clear to me whether you want to solve your problem with
VMS or some Unix variant.  Anyway, here's some info on VMS, xterm and
dxterm.

The VMS equivalent to .Xdefaults is DECW$XDEFAULTS.DAT.  By default
that's in your login directory although you can redefine the logical
DECW$USER_DEFAULTS to change the location.  Likewise, the VMS
equivalent to the XTerm resource file is XTERM.DAT.  Putting the line:

	XTerm*vt100.geometry:       132x40+500+400

in XTERM.DAT will give you a 132 column by 40 line vt100 window at
(500,400).  Alternately, the same command as in Unix:

	xterm -geometry 132x40+500+400

will yield the same results (assuming you have xterm defined as a
foreign command or you have VMS 6.2 or newer and the DCL$PATH logical
locates the image).  Since this is a VMS command, case isn't important
(unless you start playing games with quotes).  Case *is* important, of
course, in the resource file.

The VMS command for creating a DXterm is CREATE/TERMINAL.  You can
set the window title and icon name by adding

	/WINDOW_ATTRIBUTES=(TITLE:"Title",ICON_NAME:"icon")

(the quotes are required only if you want to preserve case or put
special characters in the title or icon name) or you can put

	DECW$TERMINAL.iconName: icon
	DECW$TERMINAL.title:    Title

in DECW$TERMINAL_DEFAULT.DAT (may also work in DECW$XDEFAULTS.DAT, I
don't know).  The title will replace the copyright on the first mouse
click in the window or after a few seconds.  You can also change the
title/icon on the fly by issuing appropriate escape sequences.

I don't know how to remove the menu bar.  I have an old message that
claims that:

	*decterm_mb*height:	1

in DECW$XDEFAULTS.DAT (or possibly DECW$TERMINAL_DEFAULT.DAT) should
work but I had no luck with it.

Btw, I'm assuming you have DECWindows Motif 1.2-3 or newer on your
VMS system.

Hth,
Dave
