Ruth Ryan <ruth@ocean.ccit.arizona.edu> writes:
> I am trying to install INFORMIX and it dies when looking for
> librt.so as follows:
> 
> /sbin/loader: Fatal Error: cannot map librt.so

When you can't find a system component, look in the subset inventories
to see what subset it is in--for example, for librt.so, do

dsr_lns101% grep librt.so /usr/.smdb./*.inv
/usr/.smdb./OSFRTDEV350.inv:0   98304   56329   3       4       100644  
   7/24/95350      f       ./usr/shlib/librt.so    none    OSFRTDEV350

which tells you that (on this system running Digital Unix 3.2G),
librt.so is in the real time development subset, OSFRTDEV350, and you
need to setld that subset from the distribution media (NB: the name
and number varies with OS version, so be sure to do the grep yourself
on the system you are installing Informix on).
