Dana McClure wrote:
> 
> I am trying to prep 2 new SCSI drives. So far I have determined the SCSI
> info, ran MAKEDEV to make the special files for rz12 and rz13. Now I am
> trying to partition the drives using DISKLABEL and the rz28 format as
> seen:
>       disklabel -r -w -t ufs /dev/rz12a rz28
> 
> I assume this is a syntax error, can anyone help?  On another note I
> wish to create a single partition using both drives. Can this be done
> with the mount command? If so what would the syntax be? Please email any
> thoughts to Dana_McClure@xn.xerox.com
> 
> Thanks
> Dana

Dana,
The correct syntax is:

       disklabel -r -w -t ufs /dev/rrz12a rz28
or
       disklabel -r -w -t ufs rz12a rz28

(this *is* made clear in the man page).

To create a single partition from both drives, I think you need AdvFS.
LSM might be an alternative (I've only used AdvFS to create multi-disk
partitions, so aren't 100% sure about LSM). Creation of AdvFS partitions
is well documented, but I can give you the details if necessary.
Regards,
John Hill
