The -O option (alongs with some others) is not necessarily supported on
other vendor's lpd systems - it's a Digital thing, so if the remote
printer is not on a Digital system it's unlikely to know what to do.
I'm currently working on a distributed printing system and have
encountered these problems, although in my case I'm using a Digital
Alpha to do the printing and adding code to the standard BSD lpd source
to give it the extra functionality when passing jobs to the Alpha's lpd
(i.e. the reverse of what you want and much easier!). I don't know how
the Digital lpd actually implements things like orientation (-O) and
paging (-K)...

