Remote printers assume that all the intelligence is handled by the remote
node.  In our case, the remote nodes are all Lantronix print servers, so
all data received is just sent down the cable to the printer.  There is no
special driver used at all.

I have set up a script which checks for the printer, (in my case HP
Laserjet) and send a small text file before and after the print file.  The
before file sends the HP codes for landscape, while the after file sends a
reset.


Also, even for local printers -Olandscape only works if the driver supports
it.  So again, send the appropraite commands for your printer before and
after.

Doug Hamilton
