Mark,
Are you running tcp_wrappers on your system?
We had a similar problem for host machines that where defined within our
/etc/hosts file but where not defined on the local DNS server.
If you are using tcpd, then your problem is probably associated with the
PARANOID option set in tcpd, when requests a second check on any
hostname. Hence the host name in your /etc/hosts file will not match a
query from your local DNS, and the request is aborted.

If this is your problem (I am unsure how sendmail is affected by tcpd),
then you can re-compile tcpd with the PARANOID option commented out, and
it should work fine.

However, we do notice that nslookup still does not work either. If you
hear of a method to fix this, we'd appreciate hearing from you.

