-1st point

D.U. uses a memory management that frees physical memory only when
needed (free list below vm-page-free-min (20 pages of 8K by default.))

That means that the page stealer won't start until this trigger.

All the memory use you see can be old part, not used anymore, of some
processes which have quite a big acivity in term of deplacement into
there own VM spaces. use ps command and track RSS field

-2d point

Memory is shared with UBC cache, which can grow up to ubc-maxpercent
(100 % of memory by default). the page stealer will first take memory
from UBC until ubc-minpercent is reached (10 or 30% of memory by
default). Find an utility called vmubc on freeware CDROM V4.0 to track
it.


To summarize, don't look at memory use at one time to see the memory
necessary to your system, check paging out activity (pages to be free
and that have been modified) and UBC trimming (system wide), and RSS and
paging activity of your big processes.

There's a documentation in D.U. standard doc and CDROM which explains
all this stuff and ways to monitor and tune memory, I/O, ...


regards,

