"Andrew Mc.Ghee" <mcghee@sun.mech.uq.edu.au> writes:

> Thanks Holger,
> We have tried compiling gcc2.7.2.2 and g77-0.5.20 but am now worried
> about seeing the following error messages appear when we compile as;
> # make bootstrap
> 
> /usr/bin/ld:
> Warning: Linking some objects which contain exception information
> sections and some which do not. This may cause fatal runtime exception
> handling problems (last obj encountered without exceptions was
> underscore.o).
> #
> 
> This error is interspersed throughout the make output. Is this error as
> serious as we think it is, is there a way around it, or is simply a
> warning that can be ignored?

It is a warning that can usually be ignored.

If you read it carefully, it is telling you that underscore.o contains
no exception information. While I have no idea what is in
underscore.c, I bet there is no executable code. If this is the case,
there is no problem.

On the other hand, if underscore.c should be producing executable
code, this indicates a real problem.

Digital C puts a dummy exception section in all objects while gcc
does not, so you should only see this warning with gcc compiled code.
-- 
