In article <01bc287c.e4464f00$39cd79a3@sabeshr.rite.com>, "Sally Beshr" <sabeshr@rite.com> writes:
|> is there any way i can configure a single ethernet interface to accomodate
|> more than one ip address on a dec alpha running osf1?

This is a frequent question.

Do "man ifconfig" and read this part:
  alias     Establishes an additional network address for this interface.
            This is sometimes useful when changing network numbers and one
            wishes to accept packets addressed to the old interface.

On Digital UNIX V4.0 and later, I believe there should be no trouble
with using several thousand aliases on one system.  On earlier releases,
you might have performance problems if you use more than few hundred
aliases.

-Jeff



