In article <33185639.65462617@news.dpro.com>, rsala@dpro.com (Raymond D. Sala) writes:

>Can someone give me a "kick start" on adding two (2) additional
>filesystems (e.i /disk2 /disk3) on two additional scsi disks on an
>Alpha 2000?

1.  Label the disks.

	disklabel -wr /dev/rrz#c type
	disklabel -wr /dev/rrz@c type

    Don't worry if "type" isn't in /etc/disktab.  Most well
    behaved disks will provide the disklabel command their
    geometry.  Note: replace # and @ with appropriate device
    numbers.

2.  Create the file system.  It doesn't get much easier than newfs.

	newfs /dev/rrz#c
	newfs /dev/rrz@c

2b. Alternately, you can use AdvFS.

	mkfdmn /dev/rz#c domain-1
	mkfdmn /dev/rz@c domain-2
	mkfset domain-1 fileset-1
	mkfset domain-2 fileset-2

2c. If you have the AdvFS utilities and want a multi-device domain:

	mkfdmn /dev/rz#c domain
	addvol /dev/rz@c domain
	mkfset domain fileset

3.  Mount the file systems

	mount /dev/rz#c /disk2
	mount /dev/rz@c /disk3

    This assume the directories are already created.  The mount
    manual page for the changes needed to mount AdvFS file systems.

4.  Edit /etc/fstab so they'll be mounted when the system boots.

>Ray Sala
