Date: 1997/03/04
Message-ID: <5fh6u2$o1@es2.es.osaka-u.ac.jp>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 222997643
References: <5fdvul$jn@es2.es.osaka-u.ac.jp>
Organization: Faculty of Engineering Science, Osaka University
Newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1


In article <5fdvul$jn@es2.es.osaka-u.ac.jp>
Jun Ushida writes:

|Hello,
|
|Please tell me how to change 'dimensions' of X Window System.
|Now 'dimensions' is 1024x768.

I recieved a answer by a e-mail from a very kind person named Jeff Payne.
(payne@solg2.bnsc.rl.ac.uk)

|Jun, Modify the /etc/dt/config/Xservers file, to read
|
|   :0   Local local@console /usr/bin/X11/X :0 -screen0 1280 -vsync 72
|    
|then reboot.

I don't have /etc/dt/confing/Xservers, 
so I copy /usr/dt/config/Xservers to /etc/dt/config/Xservers 
and modify the file.

Finally I can use X Window System with higher dimensions.
Thank you very much.



--
Jun Ushida
ushida@kronos.mp.es.osaka-u.ac.jp



