> I just received a warning message claiming that there is a security
> bug in /usr/sbin/dop.  Has anybody else heard of this?  Does anybody
> know what dop is suppose to do?

I don't know what /usr/sbin/dop is supposed to do, but there is a
trivial shell script that exploits it to allow any unprivileged user to
get a root shell.  Remove the setuid bit from dop immediately with
"chmod u-s /usr/sbin/dop"; it can't be _that_ important to your system.

