- Update Installations are Safe with Patches
- New Patch Procedure 'dupatch'

Colin Cargill wrote:
> 
> Quoting a Digital document:
> 
> "BLITZ TITLE: Clarification on Upgrade Installs - Digital UNIX Patches
> 
>       DEPARTMENT: Digital UNIX Problem Management    CROSS REFERENCE #'s:
>                                                      (PRISM/TIME/CLD#'s)


Update Installations are Safe with Patches

The quoted support blitz entitled "Clarification on Upgrade Installs -
Digital UNIX Patches" was erroneous and has been reissued.  The Blitz
was meant to apply to setld upgrades with a Sparse Inventory Digital 
UNIX kit, NOT Update Installations with Full Inventory Digital UNIX
kits.   More infomation regarding these two types of kits is located at:

 http://www.zk3.dec.com/dupatchwww/system-upgrades.txt


An Update Installation is not affected by patches since it will load a
full copy of Digital UNIX onto the system and overwrite any previous
patches that may have existed.  Any new patches provided by DIGITAL
for the new release should be applied following the Update
Installation.


New Patch Procedure 'dupatch'

A new patch delivery mechanism has been released for Digital UNIX
V3.2C, and V4.0B, and is soon to be released for V3.2D, V3.2E,
V3.2F, V3.2G, V4.0, and V4.0A.  Patches will be distributed as tar
files which include a utility called 'dupatch' and a number of patch
subsets.  The 'dupatch' utility can be used to load, delete, and view
installed patches.  This new procedure will provide a much more robust
mechanism for managing patches on a Digital UNIX system.


