A.F. de Bruijn (a.f.dbruijn@sir.dgsm.minvenw.nl) wrote:
: Hallo
: we are working on a aplha 2100-250 with 512mb memory and currently we get
: the message: vmunix: task table is full
: in the /var/adm/messages file.
: when a user tries to start something he gets the message:
: can not fork to many processes.
: the program top gives 275 processes, and there a around 45 users logged in.
: 
: In the sysconfigtab there is a parameter maxusers=64

For DUX 3.x, yes edit /sys/HOSTNAME/sysconfigtab and change maxusers to 256 or so.  
Then doconfig (to build kernel), cp vmunix /, reboot.

FYI we also change /etc/sysconfigtab with the following:

pts:
        nptys=1026

proc:
        # The user CGI has to run many many processes, so we make this
        # a high value - 512
        max-proc-per-user=512
        per-proc-stack-size=1073741824
        max-per-proc-stack-size=1073741824
        per-proc-data-size=1073741824

NOTE: DUX 4.0B moved the maxusers from /sys/HOSTNAME/sysconfigtab to???
Just realized I forgot / didn't figure this out yet on on our 4.0B box...

Good luck.


Curt Smith
curts@compgen.com




